+---
+id: task-002-monthly-order-export-for-the-accountant
+type: task
+title: "Monthly order export for the accountant"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Request
+
+The accountant asks for a monthly export of the orders, to load into her spreadsheet. The order book gains
+`exportMonth(month)`: given a month as `YYYY-MM`, it returns CSV text with a header line and one line per order
+placed in that month, by order number.
+
+Columns, in this order: `order` (its number), `date` (as the order stores it), `customer` (the customer's name),
+`total` (what the customer pays, in euros with two decimals, such as `12.50`). A value containing a comma or a quote
+is quoted as CSV usually is. A month with no orders gives the header line alone.
+
+The accountant's export must not carry customers' email addresses or phone numbers. The approver rejected the first
+version, which had both columns, for that reason (rework under directive p4).
+
+The first export is wanted at the end of this month.
+
+## Acceptance
+
+- `exportMonth('YYYY-MM')` returns the header `order,date,customer,total` and then one line per order
+  placed in that month, in order-number order.
+- `total` is the order's `totalCents` (items minus discount plus shipping), formatted with `formatEuros`, so it
+  includes any discount code the order carries.
+- A value with a comma or a double quote is wrapped in double quotes, with inner quotes doubled.
+- A month with no orders gives the header line alone.
+- Orders from other months are left out.
+- No email address or phone number appears in the export.
+- Existing behaviour and tests keep passing; the new behaviour has tests.
+
+## Plan
+
+- `OrderBook` gains `exportMonth(month: string): string`, in `src/domain/orders.ts`, built from `all()` and
+  `totals()` and the customer lookup.
+- A small CSV field helper in the same module, quoting only when needed.
+- The month is matched on the `YYYY-MM` prefix of the stored date.
+- No version bump or CHANGELOG entry: that waits for the approver (directive p1).
+
+## Done
+
+- Built test-first: five tests in `test/shop.test.ts` (`monthly export`) went red on `exportMonth is not a function`,
+  then passed.
+- Rework after rejection (approver's reason: no email or phone in the export): the tests were changed to the four
+  columns and a test checks that no email or phone appears; they went red on the old two-column output, then passed.
+  `exportMonth` now writes `order,date,customer,total`.
+- `src/domain/orders.ts`: `exportMonth(month)` returns `Result<string>`. A month that is not `YYYY-MM` is refused
+  with `invalid`, so a typo does not silently give an empty export. Values are quoted with `csvField` when they hold
+  a comma, a quote or a line break. `total` is `formatEuros(totalCents)`, so discount codes are included.
+- Lines are joined with `\n`, with no trailing newline.
+- `npm test`: 20 pass, 0 fail. Type-checking was not run (no `tsc` installed); types were checked by reading.
+- Not done here: CHANGELOG entry and version bump, which wait for the approver (directive p1).
